        "type": "FINDING",
        "position": 0,
        "title": null,
        "content": null,
        "reportFindingId": "f0000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000000i1",
        "reportFinding": {
          "id": "f0000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000000i1",
          "reportId": "r0000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000000ir",
          "title": "Business email compromise via adversary-in-the-middle phishing",
          "severity": "CRITICAL",
          "description": "An attacker phished the session token of **jsmith@example.com** through an adversary-in-the-middle page, then used it from `203.0.113.45` to read mail and create a forwarding rule.\n\nMFA was satisfied by the stolen session, so it did not stop the sign-in.",
          "impact": "Finance correspondence, including two pending wire instructions, was readable by the attacker for about 26 hours.",
          "recommendation": "1. Require phishing-resistant MFA (FIDO2) for finance roles.\n2. Block mailbox auto-forwarding to external domains.\n3. Alert on inbox rules that forward or delete.",
          "reference": "https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1557/",
          "tags": [
            "BEC",
            "AiTM"
          ],
          "affectedSystems": [
